# Docker build context excludes.

#

# docker/Dockerfile and docker/Dockerfile.nginx both `COPY . .` from the repo

# root, so anything not listed here is uploaded to the daemon and can end up in

# the image. Without this file the context carries node_modules (host binaries,

# wrong platform), a stale dist/, and the entire .git history.

#

# DO NOT exclude public/ or docker/. Vite copies public/ into dist/, which is how

# /config/app.json reaches the running container — excluding it builds fine and

# then fails at boot in appConfig.initialize() (see docs/DECISIONS.md,

# 2026-08-17). Dockerfile.nginx COPYs docker/nginx.conf out of the context.

node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
.git
supabase/.temp

# Local and editor state

*.local
*.log
.codegraph
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store

# Not needed to build the app

.claude
.agents
.github
.gitea
docs
*.md
.dockerignore
dockerbuild.bat
